\f0\fs28\b Yamaha Soundbar (umbrella driver)\b0\fs20\par
\par
IP driver for Yamaha soundbars built on the Linkplay platform (currently YAS-209). Presents to Control4 as a Receiver (power, volume, mute, input, transport).\par
\par
\b Control Method\b0  (property)\par
\bullet  \b IP\b0  \endash  implemented. Volume/mute/transport use the soundbar's UPnP service (no setup). Power and input use the soundbar's local API and require \b Owner Approved = Yes\b0  (see below).\par
\bullet  \b IR / Serial\b0  \endash  placeholders for a later release. (The shipping default will be IR.)\par
\par
\b Setup (IP)\b0\par
1. Add the driver, place it in the soundbar's room.\par
2. Set \b Model\b0  and \b IP Address\b0  (use a DHCP reservation on the bar).\par
3. In Connections, bind AUDIO/VIDEO OUTPUT to the room; wire real sources to the HDMI/Optical/TV/Bluetooth inputs.\par
4. Volume, mute and transport work immediately.\par
\par
\b Owner Approved (power + input over IP)\b0\par
Power on/off and input switching over IP use a client certificate that authenticates to the soundbar's local control API. Enabling this is the \b equipment owner's\b0  decision. Leave \b Owner Approved = No\b0  unless the owner has consented; the driver still provides volume/mute/transport, and power/input can be handled by IR. Set to \b Yes\b0  only with the owner's approval.\par
\par
\b Notes\b0\par
Streaming sources (Spotify, Alexa) are driven by their own apps. This driver exposes transport (play/pause/next/previous) as Actions.\par
\par
